From: Codex <noreply@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm: sdp: require explicit experimental enable property

The firmware-derived SDP DRM node is deliberately disabled. Keep an
additional software interlock when a developer later changes status to
"okay": the driver must not map display MMIO or request its IRQ unless the
same DT node has samsung,enable-experimental-kms.

This is a project safety policy, not a hardware property. It makes a future
hardware trial a conscious, reviewable DT change and leaves disabled nodes
entirely inert. It neither establishes panel timing, IRQ polarity, nor the
GPU clock/supply path. No hardware tests.

Signed-off-by: Codex <noreply@openai.com>
---
 .../bindings/display/samsung,sdp-drm.yaml          | 52 +++++++++++++++++++++
 drivers/gpu/drm/sdp/sdp_drm.c                       |  9 ++++
 2 files changed, 61 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/samsung,sdp-drm.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/samsung,sdp-drm.yaml
new file mode 100644
index 000000000000..1f4fabb9e812
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/samsung,sdp-drm.yaml
@@ -0,0 +1,52 @@
+# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only OR BSD-2-Clause
+%YAML 1.2
+---
+$id: http://devicetree.org/schemas/display/samsung,sdp-drm.yaml#
+$schema: http://devicetree.org/meta-schemas/core.yaml#
+
+title: Samsung SDP Nike-L GP-plane DRM/KMS controller
+
+maintainers:
+  - Q60T Linux porting project <noreply@example.invalid>
+
+description: |
+  The Samsung SDP Nike-L boot-logo pipeline exposes OSD, GP, mixer, QE, GA,
+  POST and TMG MMIO regions. The runtime driver currently owns only the GP
+  scanout plane and mixer VBlank path. It is experimental and requires an
+  explicit software interlock in addition to status = "okay".
+
+properties:
+  compatible:
+    const: samsung,sdp-drm
+
+  reg:
+    minItems: 7
+    maxItems: 7
+
+  interrupts:
+    minItems: 2
+    maxItems: 2
+
+  samsung,enable-experimental-kms:
+    type: boolean
+    description: |
+      Required by the Linux driver before it maps MMIO or requests the VBlank
+      IRQ. This is a project safety interlock, not a hardware description.
+
+required:
+  - compatible
+  - reg
+  - interrupts
+
+additionalProperties: true
+
+examples:
+  - |
+    drm@5d0000 {
+        compatible = "samsung,sdp-drm";
+        reg = <0x5d0000 0x4000>, <0x5d4000 0x4000>,
+              <0x5d8000 0x4000>, <0x5dc000 0x40000>,
+              <0x580000 0x4000>, <0x700000 0xd000>,
+              <0xc00000 0x20000>;
+        interrupts = <0 47 0>, <0 102 0>;
+        status = "disabled";
+    };
+...
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/sdp/sdp_drm.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/sdp/sdp_drm.c
index a08d908f0b4c..6029053e8072 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/sdp/sdp_drm.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/sdp/sdp_drm.c
@@ -519,6 +519,15 @@ static int sdp_drm_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	struct resource *res;
 	int irq, ret, i;
 
+	/*
+	 * status = "okay" alone must never turn an experimental display path
+	 * into a hardware trial. Keep this interlock before any MMIO mapping.
+	 */
+	if (!of_property_read_bool(pdev->dev.of_node,
+				   "samsung,enable-experimental-kms"))
+		return dev_err_probe(&pdev->dev, -EPERM,
+			"experimental KMS is not explicitly enabled in DT\n");
+
 	sdp = devm_drm_dev_alloc(&pdev->dev, &sdp_drm_driver,
 				 struct sdp_drm_device, drm);
 	if (IS_ERR(sdp))
-- 
2.43.0
